From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:58:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): reset ready age on manual and spend promotion
 [daveey]

A spend-triaged card promoted after a three-hour hold must start a new ready
interval. Centralize ready-entry clock kinds and share the floor with diagnostic,
chat-wait prefilter and admission scoring, retaining claimed/spawned observations
and the existing conditional continued/unused-grant/run-end behavior.

Why-chain
- A hub card woke, entered spend triage, and was later promoted_manual after
  a multi-hour hold. Seconds afterward its chat_wait_unclaimed notice still
  used the original wake time as ready_since and reported the whole hold as
  ready age; the card was claimed shortly after.
- ready_since uses _last_ready_entry_ts, whose hand-maintained floor omitted
  promoted_manual, written by both CLI promote and spend_promote.
- Separate lists registered the new path inconsistently. There was no shared
  ready-entry registry and no ready -> triage -> promote age regression.
- Previous fixes (wake/claim, run end) and the
  unused-grant exclusion each fixed one input, not registry completeness.
- The same stale floor inflated admission age at 25 points/minute (uncapped),
  starvation clocks and other wait diagnostics; no weights/thresholds/wording
  or placement change is made here.

Writer audit
- Include promoted_manual: kanban_db_promote.promote_task and
  kanban_spend_promote.apply explicitly UPDATE status='ready'.
- Include triage_swept: sweep_stale_triage explicitly writes ready.
- Include containment_released: resume_local writes the released resume status,
  including ready, then appends that event.
- Include review_reopened: reopen_review_task computes landing ready/todo and
  writes it before the event.
- Include reopened: reopen_done_task computes ready/todo/review and writes it.
- Include changes_requested: request_changes ends review into ready/todo.
- Exclude status: current lifecycle writer is descendant invalidation to todo,
  not a ready entry. continued stays separately payload-gated on status=ready.
- Keep created, promoted, reclaimed, unblocked, continuation_woken,
  condition_met, wake_probe_stale, wake_check_stale, owner_restart_lost.
- Requeue BLOCK_RELEASE_EVENTS, terminal_guard REOPEN_KINDS, lanes admission
  history and capacity_metrics counting are different policies (including
  payload-sensitive events), not the ready-age clock. Their memberships and
  behavior are deliberately unchanged; substituting/unioning the clock registry
  would change unrelated behavior.

Tests
Base: 5a584cd3fa06e58766a20c1acf5e5b4997305b9c.
Both real promotion paths fail on baseline consumers; six missing-kind table
rows also fail (8 failures total). New tests check zero admission age and no
notice before threshold, one notice at threshold and deduplication afterward.
The independently enumerated 15-kind floor table covers the audited entries.
An AST inventory of status-writing functions rejects new unregistered literal
event kinds, including parameterized-status SQL; four negative controls prove
new-kind discovery with SQL whitespace and facade/bare-call variants.
All existing tests are unmodified: no old-floor assertion rewritten.
The eight required suites recount at this base to exactly the supplied counts:
ready_wait_checkpoint 31, hub_admission 150, score_sources 19,
starvation_index 13, spend_promote 29, wait_notice_board_counts 26,
stranded_reroute 26, history_ready_reductions 81. All pass.
Existing claimed/spawned/unblocked/run-end/unused-grant regression suites are
retained, including ready_wait_restart_floor (10 cases).
Full scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks green.

Post-install acceptance remains on the implementation card: replay events/runs
cut just after a promotion, expecting ready_since to equal the promotion time
(not the original wake time), and list currently-ready cards whose floor changes.
Read-only hub checks only; stop and post evidence if replay fails.

